  "historical_output_text": " When I turned thirty-five last October my life felt like one continuous struggle.\n\nAfter my last job I had been trying and trying again for new opportunities. It became an exercise that consumed all free thought in me; every spare minute and energy that could have once found me at my best was lost and instead spent trying so hard for an uncertain end that I became bitter. It wasn'T just a feeling I felt but something real, I lost touch. \n\nThe only solvace I ever found, was in reading fiction; a way, to lose all touch of the outside. My books were always the most important and my only escape to other lives; they allowed my imagination free range and were like the most real dreams I'd ever known; the only real connection and joy. And then the book came. A story by the most unlikely author; a man",
